  "output": {
    "answer": "It means the model reviewing a lane's output has to be a stronger tier than the model that built it, never a peer — the ordering runs haiku to sonnet to opus to my strongest model. A sonnet-tier build lane gets an opus-tier reviewer, for example. And the review can't just say 'looks good' — it has to state plainly what it checked, like a count, a spot-check with exact lines, or a re-run of the gate's command. My strongest model is the one writing the briefs and judging results, while I make the final calls.",
